<TD VALIGN=top>
<TABLE BORDER=0 CELLSPACING=12 CELLPADDING=0>
<FORM>
<TR><TD><SPAN STYLE="color:#336699;font-size:18px;font-weight:bold">TimerMod</SPAN><BR>By <B>Arista</B> of the Seventh Hammer</TD></TR>

<TR><TD>TimerMod is an EverQuest user interface modification that integrates a timer into your display.</TD></TR>
<TR><TD CLASS=note>
	Example uses:<BR>
	<LI>Buff/debuff duration</LI>
	<LI>Activated ability re-use time
	<LI>Discipline duration/availability</LI>
	<LI>Mesmerize spells</LI>
	<LI>Damage over time spells</LI>
	<LI>Spawn cycles</LI>
	<LI>Adventure deadlines</LI>
	<LI>Elapsed play time</LI>
</TD></TR>
<TR><TD HEIGHT=1 BGCOLOR=#336699><IMG SRC="images/336699.gif" WIDTH=1 HEIGHT=1></TD></TR>

<TR><TD CLASS=subsectiontitle>Slider Timer</TD></TR>
<TR><TD><IMG SRC="images/timers_normal.jpg"> <IMG SRC="images/timers_faded.jpg"> <IMG SRC="images/timers_compact_faded.jpg"></TR></TD>
<TR><TD HEIGHT=1 BGCOLOR=#CCCCCC><IMG SRC="images/cccccc.gif" WIDTH=1 HEIGHT=1></TD></TR>
<TR><TD><SPAN CLASS=feature>Time Marker</SPAN><BR>The slider timer never needs to be reset. When you want to start timing, simply move the slider to mark the current position of the bar. It will take the bar exactly one full duration of the timer to reach the slider again.</TD></TR>
<TR><TD HEIGHT=1 BGCOLOR=#CCCCCC><IMG SRC="images/cccccc.gif" WIDTH=1 HEIGHT=1></TD></TR>
<TR><TD><SPAN CLASS=feature>Multiple Timers</SPAN><BR>Choose the number of timers to include, from 1 timer up to 12 timers. Specify how many rows/columns to use.</TD></TR>
<TR><TD HEIGHT=1 BGCOLOR=#CCCCCC><IMG SRC="images/cccccc.gif" WIDTH=1 HEIGHT=1></TD></TR>
<TR><TD><SPAN CLASS=feature>Custom Label and Duration</SPAN><BR>Specify a custom name and duration for each timer, corresponding to the event you want to time.</TD></TR>
<TR><TD HEIGHT=1 BGCOLOR=#CCCCCC><IMG SRC="images/cccccc.gif" WIDTH=1 HEIGHT=1></TD></TR>
<TR><TD><SPAN CLASS=feature>Multiple Colors</SPAN><BR>Each bar is color-coded for easy identification. There are 5 colors to choose from.</TD></TR>
<TR><TD HEIGHT=1 BGCOLOR=#CCCCCC><IMG SRC="images/cccccc.gif" WIDTH=1 HEIGHT=1></TD></TR>
<TR><TD><SPAN CLASS=feature>Slider Movement</SPAN><BR>Simply drag the slider to position it. You can also click on either side of the slider to move it (large increments), and in the full version, use the buttons to move the slider (small increments).</TD></TR>
<TR><TD HEIGHT=1 BGCOLOR=#CCCCCC><IMG SRC="images/cccccc.gif" WIDTH=1 HEIGHT=1></TD></TR>
<TR><TD><SPAN CLASS=feature>Customizable Graphics</SPAN><BR>Create your own custom skin for the timer, or choose from skins submitted by other users.</TD></TR>
<TR><TD HEIGHT=1 BGCOLOR=#CCCCCC><IMG SRC="images/cccccc.gif" WIDTH=1 HEIGHT=1></TD></TR>
<TR><TD><SPAN CLASS=feature>Other Options</SPAN><BR>Specify the text color for your timer, and how the bar is animated. Also, choose between the full version and the compact version (for saving screen space).</TD></TR>
<TR><TD HEIGHT=1 BGCOLOR=#CCCCCC><IMG SRC="images/cccccc.gif" WIDTH=1 HEIGHT=1></TD></TR>
<TR><TD><INPUT TYPE=button VALUE="Customize Slider Timer" ONCLICK="location.href='customize.asp'"></TD></TR>

<TR><TD HEIGHT=1 BGCOLOR=#336699><IMG SRC="images/336699.gif" WIDTH=1 HEIGHT=1></TD></TR>

<TR><TD CLASS=subsectiontitle>Dial/Digital Timer</TD></TR>
<TR><TD><IMG SRC="images/timer_normal.jpg"> <IMG SRC="images/timer_faded.jpg"></TR></TD>
<TR><TD HEIGHT=1 BGCOLOR=#CCCCCC><IMG SRC="images/cccccc.gif" WIDTH=1 HEIGHT=1></TD></TR>
<TR><TD><SPAN CLASS=feature>Tick Dial</SPAN><BR>The tick dial represents one minute, divided into 10 in-game ticks (6-second intervals). Useful for visually eyeballing the duration of short-term events.</TD></TR>
<TR><TD HEIGHT=1 BGCOLOR=#CCCCCC><IMG SRC="images/cccccc.gif" WIDTH=1 HEIGHT=1></TD></TR>
<TR><TD><SPAN CLASS=feature>Tick Marker</SPAN><BR>The tick marker allows you mark any tick on the dial, to help keep track of an event. Simply click on one of the dial's number labels to mark the beginning or end of an event.</TD></TR>
<TR><TD HEIGHT=1 BGCOLOR=#CCCCCC><IMG SRC="images/cccccc.gif" WIDTH=1 HEIGHT=1></TD></TR>
<TR><TD><SPAN CLASS=feature>Digital Timer</SPAN><BR>The digital timer displays hours, minutes, and seconds, and can counts up to 10 hours (configurable). Useful for timing the duration of long-term events.</TD></TR>
<TR><TD HEIGHT=1 BGCOLOR=#CCCCCC><IMG SRC="images/cccccc.gif" WIDTH=1 HEIGHT=1></TD></TR>
<TR><TD><SPAN CLASS=feature>Timer Reset</SPAN><BR>The digital timer can be reset to 0:00:00 at any time by reloading the UI with a macro.</TD></TR>
<TR><TD HEIGHT=1 BGCOLOR=#CCCCCC><IMG SRC="images/cccccc.gif" WIDTH=1 HEIGHT=1></TD></TR>
<TR><TD><INPUT TYPE=button VALUE="Customize Dial/Digital Timer" ONCLICK="location.href='customize2.asp'"></TD></TR>

<TR><TD HEIGHT=1 BGCOLOR=#336699><IMG SRC="images/336699.gif" WIDTH=1 HEIGHT=1></TD></TR>

<TR><TD CLASS=subsectiontitle>Additional Features</TD></TR>
<TR><TD HEIGHT=1 BGCOLOR=#CCCCCC><IMG SRC="images/cccccc.gif" WIDTH=1 HEIGHT=1></TD></TR>
<TR><TD><SPAN CLASS=feature>Window Selection</SPAN><BR>The timer can occupy the unused window of your choice. Choose from 14 different windows in the UI.</TD></TR>
<TR><TD HEIGHT=1 BGCOLOR=#CCCCCC><IMG SRC="images/cccccc.gif" WIDTH=1 HEIGHT=1></TD></TR>
<TR><TD><SPAN CLASS=feature>Multiple Windows</SPAN><BR>Multiple timer windows can co-exist. You can configure one set of timers that you use frequently, and another set for special circumstances.</TD></TR>
<TR><TD HEIGHT=1 BGCOLOR=#CCCCCC><IMG SRC="images/cccccc.gif" WIDTH=1 HEIGHT=1></TD></TR>
<TR><TD><SPAN CLASS=feature>Window Toggle</SPAN><BR>The timer window can be shown/hidden at any time by pressing the window's configurable hot key.</TD></TR>
<TR><TD HEIGHT=1 BGCOLOR=#CCCCCC><IMG SRC="images/cccccc.gif" WIDTH=1 HEIGHT=1></TD></TR>
<TR><TD><SPAN CLASS=feature>Window Fade</SPAN><BR>The fade level of the timer window is configurable using the right-mouse menu, like any other window.</TD></TR>
<TR><TD HEIGHT=1 BGCOLOR=#CCCCCC><IMG SRC="images/cccccc.gif" WIDTH=1 HEIGHT=1></TD></TR>

</FORM>
</TABLE>
</TD>
